# Redirect rules live here, not in netlify.toml.
#
# netlify.toml is not applied on this site in production — verified 2026-08-04:
# /terms, /privacy, and /app all returned 200 (the SPA catch-all below) instead
# of the redirects declared there, even though `netlify dev --dir build` honours
# them locally. This file is demonstrably honoured in production, so it is the
# single source of truth until the netlify.toml issue is resolved.
#
# Order matters: Netlify applies the first matching rule, so the SPA catch-all
# MUST stay last or it swallows everything below it.

# Branded acquisition link. Anything handed out off-site (bio links, ads, QR
# codes) should use https://delirio.fit/app, or https://delirio.fit/app/<token>
# for a short per-source campaign link (e.g. /app/iris in an Instagram bio).
#
# A 200 rewrite to an interstitial rather than a 302 straight to Apple: on iOS
# the OS intercepts an apps.apple.com navigation to open the App Store app and
# cancels it in the browser, so a bare 302 leaves behind a tab that never
# rendered anything — a white page when the user switches back. app.html paints
# first, then hands off, then sends the tab to the landing page. It also
# forwards ?pt=/?ct=/?mt= (or any other query string) to Apple untouched, and
# expands /app/<token> into the same shape using a hardcoded provider token —
# see the PROVIDER_TOKEN comment in app.html.
/app/*      /app.html    200
/app        /app.html    200

# Legacy legal paths.
/terms      /terms-of-service     301!
/privacy    /privacy-policy       301!

# The sitemap and canonical tags use no trailing slash. Keep the alternate
# directory form from becoming a second indexable URL for pre-rendered pages.
/ai-fitness-coach/          /ai-fitness-coach          301!
/adaptive-workout-planner/  /adaptive-workout-planner  301!
/voice-workout-coach/       /voice-workout-coach       301!
/workout-form-feedback/     /workout-form-feedback     301!
/support/                   /support                   301!
/terms-of-service/          /terms-of-service          301!
/privacy-policy/            /privacy-policy            301!
/data-deletion/             /data-deletion             301!

# Public React routes are pre-rendered during the build, so no SPA catch-all is
# needed. Netlify serves a genuine 404 (and this repository's 404.html) for an
# unknown URL instead of returning the home-page shell with a 200 status.
